{"id":"doc:packages/cli/skills/crib-enrich/SKILL.md#phase-0-the-scope-picker-first-thing-once-per-session","kind":"doc-section","file":"packages/cli/skills/crib-enrich/SKILL.md","heading":"Phase 0 — the scope picker (first thing, once per session)","level":2,"anchor":"phase-0-the-scope-picker-first-thing-once-per-session","span":{"start":23,"end":56},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:2b8624436b17076a2701f9f0b2d39bf2fbbe7609c1fb3bb1ba9ace902c38105e","meta":{"codeRefs":["mcp__knowledge-crib__enrich_status","{ scopes: true }","totalPending <= threshold","threshold","scopes","totalPending > threshold","scopes.length > 0","enrich_next","This repo has <totalPending> pending LLM targets across 4 layers (symbol: <s> pending, file: <f> pending, cluster: <c> pending, system: 1 total), exceeding the recommended threshold of <threshold>. At 4 items/batch that is ~<totalPending/4> batches — enriching everything unattended is not realistic. Which module should I enrich first?\n\nTop-5 modules by pending symbols (the parenthesized counts are TOTAL symbols/files/clusters in that prefix;","is pending symbols only):\n  1. <scopes[0].pathPrefix>   — <scopes[0].pending> pending  (<scopes[0].symbols> symbols, <scopes[0].files> files, <scopes[0].clusters> clusters)\n  2. <scopes[1].pathPrefix>   — <scopes[1].pending> pending  (...)\n  3. <scopes[2].pathPrefix>   — <scopes[2].pending> pending  (...)\n  4. <scopes[3].pathPrefix>   — <scopes[3].pending> pending  (...)\n  5. <scopes[4].pathPrefix>   — <scopes[4].pending> pending  (...)\n\nOptions:\n  • Type a number (1–5) to scope to that module.\n  • Type a path prefix (e.g. packages/cli/src) for a finer scope.\n  • Type 'list clusters <number>' to refine by cluster inside a module first.\n  • Type 'full' to enrich the whole repo (not recommended — ~<totalPending/4> batches).\n\nI'll wait for your choice before proceeding.","**Scope carry:** once the user picks, remember the scope for the rest of this","session and pass","to EVERY","+","call. The scope lives in your prompt context, not server-side. Resolve the choice:\n- A number","→",".\n- A custom prefix string →",".\n-","→ call",". This returns the **pending cluster work items** under that prefix; each item's","is a cluster id (e.g.","). Show them, let the user pick one, then set","(the","-prefixed id, or its bare slug, both accepted).\n-","→ no scope (undefined).\n\nIf a new","turn cannot find the scope in context, **re-call","This","repo","has","totalPending","pending","LLM","targets","across","layers","symbol","file","cluster","system","total","exceeding","the","recommended","of","At","items/batch","that","is","totalPending/4","batches","enriching","everything","unattended","not","realistic.","Which","module","should","enrich","first","Top","modules","by","symbols","parenthesized","counts","are","TOTAL","symbols/files/clusters","in","prefix","only","1.",".pathPrefix",".pending",".symbols",".files","files",".clusters","clusters","2.","...","3.","4.","5.","Options","Type","number","to","scope","module.","path","e.g.","packages/cli/src","for","finer","scope.","list","refine","inside","first.","full","whole","ll","wait","your","choice","before","proceeding."],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:packages/cli/skills/crib-enrich/SKILL.md#phase-1-one-batch-author-save-stop-the-loop-per-turn","kind":"doc-section","file":"packages/cli/skills/crib-enrich/SKILL.md","heading":"Phase 1 — one batch, author, save, stop (the loop, per turn)","level":2,"anchor":"phase-1-one-batch-author-save-stop-the-loop-per-turn","span":{"start":57,"end":79},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:dbda65cee4c74a30b558d89ec92ab305985d042ff6d240bae608a58e853aafbb","meta":{"codeRefs":["s = enrich_status({ ...(scope? {scope} : {}) })\nif s.scopeEmpty:  print \"No pending targets under '<scope.pathPrefix>'. Check the path prefix.\" and re-present the picker; STOP.\nif s.done:        report completion (see below) and STOP. Do NOT call enrich_next.\nbatch = enrich_next({ ...(scope? {scope} : {}), limit: 4 })     # grounded seed + schema per item\n# Server-side zero-progress guard (source of truth, survives context compaction):\nif batch.zeroProgress || batch.batchId === lastBatchId:  break + report zero-progress (see rule 2). Do NOT author.\nlastBatchId = batch.batchId\nitems = []\nfor item in batch.items: items.push(author(item))              # YOU reason + author (see contract)\nresult = enrich_save({ batchId: batch.batchId, items })        # server validates + persists\nreport: layer, accepted/rejected, droppedEdges, batch.remaining, overall done\nSTOP — return to the user. Re-run /crib-enrich to continue.","- **Layers run in order:**","→",".","tells you which is next; never jump ahead — higher layers'","payload contains the saved child analyses you synthesize from. **Under a scope,","excludes","** (system is whole-repo only) — a scoped run ends at the cluster layer.\n- **Resumable:** already-","targets are skipped;","reports the first","layer. Just call","again next turn.\n- **Batched:**","(default 4, max 25) bounds tokens per turn. Process one batch per turn and report progress.\n- **","** in each batch tells the user how many are left in that layer.\n- **Rejected items:** if","returns",", note them; the next turn's","enrich_status","...","scope","if","s.scopeEmpty","print","No","pending","targets","under","scope.pathPrefix","Check","the","path","prefix.","and","re","present","picker","STOP.","s.done","report","completion","see","below","Do","NOT","call","enrich_next.","batch","enrich_next","limit","grounded","seed","schema","per","item","Server","side","zero","progress","guard","source","of","truth","survives","context","compaction","batch.zeroProgress","batch.batchId","lastBatchId","break","rule","author.","items","for","in","batch.items","items.push","author","YOU","reason","contract","result","enrich_save","batchId","server","validates","persists","layer","accepted/rejected","droppedEdges","batch.remaining","overall","done","STOP","return","to","user.","Re","run","/crib","enrich","continue."],"links":[]}}
